title: A party argues about who its leader is

@bielan_rebellion
# prose-audit: Grade A — The leadership dispute is staged as the procedural absurdity it was and as the political fight underneath it, with the size of each wing taken from what the 2020 crisis actually did to Porozumienie rather than from the date.
call: poland_normalize
title: Porozumienie discovers it may not have a leader
subtitle: Bielan claims Gowin's term expired years ago; the argument is about paperwork and about which camp the party belongs to
face-image: img/poland/events/jaroslaw-gowin-2015.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.bielan_rebellion_done = 1;
Q.bielan_rebellion_open = 1;
const cohesion = Math.max(0, Number(Q.porozumienie_cohesion_2020) || 51);
const standing = Math.max(0, Number(Q.gowin_standing) || 55);
// How much of the party the rebellion can plausibly reach. A Gowin who came
// out of 2020 intact has fewer people willing to say he was never the leader.
Q.bielan_claim_strength = Math.max(10, Math.min(90, Math.round(
    46 + (60 - Math.min(60, cohesion)) * 0.7 - (standing - 55) * 0.5 +
    (Q.emilewicz_left_porozumienie ? 8 : 0) +
    (Q.gowin_returned_2020 ? -10 : 12)
)));
Q.porozumienie_status =
    "United Right junior partner disputing who leads it";
const porozumienie = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "porozumienie";
});
if (porozumienie) {
    // The 2019 list opened with eighteen Porozumienie MPs. By this dispute
    // only the twelve-person parliamentary core used by the subsequent split
    // remains; the other mandates have stayed inside the PiS family.
    const openingCount = Math.max(0, Number(porozumienie.mp_count) || 0);
    const currentCount = Math.min(openingCount, 12);
    porozumienie.mp_count = currentCount;
    porozumienie.sejm_mps = currentCount;
    const pisParty = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
        return record.id == "pis_party";
    });
    if (pisParty && openingCount > currentCount) {
        pisParty.mp_count = Math.max(0, Number(pisParty.mp_count) || 0) +
            openingCount - currentCount;
        pisParty.sejm_mps = pisParty.mp_count;
    }
    porozumienie.cohesion = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(cohesion - Q.bielan_claim_strength / 6)
    );
    porozumienie.legal_status = "allied party with a disputed leadership";
}
Q.news_headline =
    "Porozumienie's deputies cannot agree who its chairman is";
!}

= March 2021 — Two chairmen, one party

**Adam Bielan** and a group around him inform the courts, the press and
Nowogrodzka that Jarosław Gowin's term as chairman of Porozumienie expired
years ago, that the congress which was supposed to renew it never lawfully sat,
and that Bielan has therefore been acting chairman for some time without anyone
noticing. Gowin's board responds by expelling him, then **Kamil Bortniczuk**,
then whoever signs the next letter.

The registry court is asked to decide which of two men may sign for a party of
eleven deputies. It will take months and it is not really the question.

The question is which camp Porozumienie belongs to. Gowin has begun saying, in
public and without much disguise, that there is space for a moderate,
pro-enterprise centre-right built with PSL and whatever **Szymon Hołownia** is
assembling. Bielan's people believe that a party which exists on the PiS list,
in the PiS club and in a PiS cabinet has no business shopping for a different
coalition, and that the deputies who follow Gowin into one will not be deputies
afterwards.

[? if bielan_claim_strength >= 60: The rebellion is not a fringe. Enough of the
party has spent a year deciding that Gowin risks their seats for arguments they
did not choose that Bielan's claim is being taken seriously by people who do
not much care whether it is true.?]
[? if bielan_claim_strength < 60: The rebellion is real and it is not yet a
majority of anything. Gowin still has the board, the name and most of the
deputies, and Bielan has a legal theory and a telephone.?]

Nowogrodzka says nothing in public and returns every call.

- @bielan_encourage
- @bielan_expose
- @bielan_ignore

@bielan_encourage
# prose-audit: Grade B — Amplifying the rebellion is the fastest route to a weaker government partner and it is charged correctly: the wing Lewica helps is the pro-PiS one, and it will still be voting with PiS in August.
title: Amplify the dispute and let the right look ungovernable
subtitle: Weakens Porozumienie now; the wing we help is the one that stays with PiS
on-arrival: {!
Q.bielan_claim_strength = Math.min(
    95,
    (Number(Q.bielan_claim_strength) || 50) + 8
);
Q.porozumienie_cohesion_2020 = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.porozumienie_cohesion_2020) || 51) - 6
);
Q.gowin_channel = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.gowin_channel) || 0) - 8);
Q.united_right_cohesion = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.united_right_cohesion) || 55) - 5
);
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left keeps the United Right's leadership farce on the front page";
!}

We put the registry filings on the record, ask in the chamber which of the two
gentlemen the government considers a coalition partner, and let the pictures do
the rest. A governing camp that cannot say who leads one of its parties is not
a governing camp that can explain a tax reform.

It works immediately and it works for Bielan, whose whole argument is that
Gowin has made Porozumienie into a liability. We are supplying the evidence.

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@bielan_expose
# prose-audit: Grade B — Naming PiS's role rather than the farce keeps the story about the government and preserves the working relationship with Gowin's wing that the 2021 minority arithmetic depends on.
title: Name who benefits and leave Gowin out of it
subtitle: Keeps Gowin reachable; a slower and less satisfying story
on-arrival: {!
Q.gowin_channel = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.gowin_channel) || 0) + 8);
Q.bielan_claim_strength = Math.max(
    5,
    (Number(Q.bielan_claim_strength) || 50) - 5
);
Q.pis_relation -= 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left asks who is paying for Porozumienie's leadership dispute";
!}

We ask the only question worth asking: why a party of eleven deputies has
suddenly discovered a constitutional crisis in its own statute in the same
month that its leader started talking about a centre-right bloc. We name
Nowogrodzka and we do not name Gowin.

It is a slower story. It also means that in eighteen months, when Gowin has
nowhere to go, there is a Lewica that did not spend 2021 laughing at him.

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@bielan_ignore
# prose-audit: Grade B — Declining the story costs nothing and gains nothing, which is the honest option when a governing party's internal law suit has no Lewica-facing consequence yet.
title: Treat it as the other camp's internal law suit
subtitle: No cost, no gain; the dispute runs on its own momentum
on-arrival: {!
Q.united_right_cohesion = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.united_right_cohesion) || 55) - 2
);
Q.news_headline =
    "A registry court is asked to decide who may sign for Porozumienie";
!}

We have a housing bill and a court case of our own. Two right-wing politicians
suing each other over a chairmanship is not a Lewica story and pretending
otherwise wastes a week.

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@republikanie_split
# prose-audit: Grade A — Partia Republikańska is assembled out of named deputies who were already recorded as leaving Gowin, its size is derived from the preceding year rather than fixed, and the event states explicitly that the split changes nothing in the parliamentary or electoral arithmetic because the new party stays inside both.
call: poland_normalize
title: The pro-government wing becomes its own party
subtitle: Partia Republikańska takes deputies from Gowin without taking a single vote from the government
face-image: img/poland/events/jaroslaw-gowin-2015.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.republikanie_event_done = 1;
const claim = Math.max(0, Number(Q.bielan_claim_strength) || 50);
const cohesion = Math.max(0, Number(Q.porozumienie_cohesion_2020) || 48);
const porozumienie = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "porozumienie";
});
const republikanie = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "republikanie";
});
const available = Math.max(0, Number(porozumienie ? porozumienie.mp_count : 11));
// The split happens unless Gowin came through 2020 with an unusually intact
// party and the rebellion never reached the deputies.
Q.republikanie_formed = (claim >= 34 && available >= 4) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.republikanie_formed) {
    Q.republikanie_seats = Math.max(2, Math.min(
        available - 3,
        Math.round(2 + claim / 22 + (60 - Math.min(60, cohesion)) / 14)
    ));
    if (porozumienie) {
        porozumienie.mp_count = Math.max(0, available - Q.republikanie_seats);
        porozumienie.sejm_mps = porozumienie.mp_count;
        porozumienie.cohesion = Math.min(
            100,
            Math.round(cohesion + 8)
        );
        porozumienie.organisation = Math.max(
            0,
            Math.round(Number(porozumienie.organisation) || 30) - 8
        );
        porozumienie.legal_status =
            "allied party reduced to its anti-Nowogrodzka wing";
    }
    if (republikanie) {
        republikanie.active = 1;
        republikanie.allied = 1;
        republikanie.independent = 1;
        // The whole point: a new party, on the same list, in the same club,
        // supporting the same government. Nothing in the count moves.
        republikanie.list_committee = "pis";
        republikanie.club = "pis";
        republikanie.support_mode = "coalition";
        republikanie.in_cabinet = 1;
        republikanie.legal_status = "allied party inside the United Right";
        republikanie.mp_count = Q.republikanie_seats;
        republikanie.sejm_mps = Q.republikanie_seats;
        republikanie.exclusive_seats = 0;
        republikanie.organisation = 26;
        republikanie.cohesion = 74;
        republikanie.relation = -6;
        republikanie.electoral_outside_option =
            "protected places on the PiS list";
    }
    const republicans = ["bielan", "bortniczuk"];
    for (const record of (Q.rival_person_records || [])) {
        if (republicans.includes(record.id)) {
            record.organisation = "republikanie";
            record.loyalty = "Bielan";
            record.status = "Partia Republikańska MP";
        }
    }
    Q.porozumienie_cohesion_2020 = Math.min(100, cohesion + 8);
    Q.gowin_standing = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.gowin_standing) || 50) - 10);
    Q.news_headline =
        "Bielan's wing leaves Gowin and stays in the government";
} else {
    Q.gowin_standing = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.gowin_standing) || 50) + 6);
    Q.porozumienie_cohesion_2020 = Math.min(100, cohesion + 6);
    if (porozumienie) {
        porozumienie.legal_status = "allied party that survived its rebellion";
    }
    Q.news_headline =
        "Gowin keeps his party; the rebels are expelled and stay put";
}
!}

= May 2021 — The split that changes no numbers

[? if republikanie_formed = 1: **Partia Republikańska** is registered with Adam
Bielan as its chairman. **[+ republikanie_seats +]** deputies leave Porozumienie
for it, along with Kamil Bortniczuk and a set of government appointments that
Gowin's board formally withdrew its recommendation from and which none of the
holders vacated. That detail is the whole lesson of the spring: a junior
coalition partner can un-recommend its own ministers, and if the prime minister
declines to act on the letter, nothing happens. The new party joins the United Right on exactly the terms Porozumienie has: the
PiS list, the PiS club, the government benches. Not one vote in the chamber
moves. The only thing that changes is that Jarosław Gowin now speaks for **[+
porozumienie_rebel_mps +]**-odd deputies instead of eleven, and Kaczyński has
demonstrated for the second time in a year that Porozumienie can be reduced
without ever losing a coalition partner.?]
[? if republikanie_formed = 0: The rebellion does not reach the deputies.
Bielan and Bortniczuk are expelled and appeal; the appeal will take a year; the
parliamentary club records no change. Gowin comes out of the spring with a
smaller board, a legal case and a party that is still his. That is a better result than he had any right to expect, and it means the
autumn will be conducted between Kaczyński and a Porozumienie that can still
count.?]

The government's majority is unchanged. Everyone in the building understands
that it is now held together by an arrangement rather than by an agreement.

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@kp_rupture
# prose-audit: Grade A — Koalicja Polska is broken by the vote its members actually split on, and the rupture moves club and committee membership without dissolving either party, establishing the framework Porozumienie and Trzecia Droga reuse later.
call: poland_normalize
title: Kukiz'15 leaves Koalicja Polska
subtitle: Two parties that shared a list in 2019 stop sharing anything; both survive the separation
face-image: img/poland/events/jaroslaw-gowin-2015.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.kp_rupture_done = 1;
Q.kukiz_left_kp = 1;
const psl = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "psl_party";
});
const kukiz = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "kukiz15";
});
// Koalicja Polska's mandates were counted as PSL's because they were filed on
// one committee. Separating the club separates the count.
const kukizMps = Math.max(0, Math.min(
    Math.round(Number(Q.psl_seats) || 30) - 1,
    Math.round(Number(kukiz ? kukiz.mp_count : 6) || 6)
));
Q.kukiz_seats = kukizMps;
Q.psl_seats = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.psl_seats) || 30) - kukizMps);
Q.psl_projected_seats = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.psl_projected_seats) || 30) - kukizMps
);
Q.kukiz_projected_seats = kukizMps;
if (kukiz) {
    kukiz.club = "kukiz15";
    kukiz.list_committee = "kukiz";
    kukiz.exclusive_seats = kukizMps;
    kukiz.mp_count = kukizMps;
    kukiz.sejm_mps = kukizMps;
    kukiz.legal_status = "independent parliamentary circle";
    kukiz.relation = Math.max(-100, (Number(kukiz.relation) || 16) - 4);
    kukiz.electoral_outside_option = "no committee agreed for the next term";
}
if (psl) {
    psl.legal_status = "party of a reduced Koalicja Polska";
    psl.cohesion = Math.min(100, (Number(psl.cohesion) || 74) + 4);
}
Q.psl_relation = Math.max(-100, (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 24) - 2);
Q.kukiz_list_committee = "kukiz";
Q.news_headline = "Kukiz'15 walks out of Koalicja Polska";
!}

= June 2021 — The end of Koalicja Polska as it was

The alliance that put **Paweł Kukiz** in the Sejm in 2019 does not survive the
European budget. Most of his deputies voted with the government on the recovery
fund while PSL voted against it, and the two organisations have spent the
months since establishing, in public, that they do not agree about the European
Union, the courts, the recovery money or each other.

Kukiz'15 registers its own parliamentary circle. **[+ kukiz_seats +]** mandates
that were counted as Koalicja Polska's are now counted as its own. PSL keeps
the name, the structures, the local government and **[+ psl_seats +]** deputies;
Kukiz keeps his deputies, his judges of peace, his referendum bill and no list
for the next election.

Neither party has been destroyed and neither has changed its leader. What has
ended is one electoral committee — which is a smaller thing than it sounds and
exactly the thing that decides who is in the next Sejm.

For us this is arithmetic before it is anything else. There is now a bloc of
**[+ kukiz_seats +]** votes in the chamber that belongs to nobody, held by a man
who does not want a ministry, in a parliament where the governing majority is
starting to require careful counting.

- @kukiz_open_channel
- @kukiz_attack_early
- @kukiz_leave_alone

@kukiz_open_channel
# prose-audit: Grade A — Opening a working relationship with Kukiz on his own institutional agenda is the only route that can later deny PiS his votes, and it costs Lewica in credibility with its own left and in nothing that PiS can be blamed for.
title: Talk to him about anti-corruption and referendums
subtitle: The only route that can outbid PiS later; our own caucus will not enjoy it
on-arrival: {!
Q.kukiz_channel = 26;
Q.kukiz_programme_credit =
    (Number(Q.kukiz_programme_credit) || 0) + 12;
Q.progressives_dissent += 4;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 2;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left and Kukiz find they want the same anti-corruption register";
!}

We start where the overlap is real rather than where it is comfortable: asset
declarations, a lobbying register, the parliamentary inquiry powers we have
wanted since 2016, and the referendum threshold. We say nothing about judges of
peace, which we think is a bad idea, and he notices that we said nothing rather
than lying.

Our progressives point out that this is a man who has spent six years as an
anti-establishment weathervane. They are right. He also has **[+ kukiz_seats
+]** votes and no coalition, and Nowogrodzka has already worked that out.

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@kukiz_attack_early
# prose-audit: Grade B — Naming him a satellite before he has become one is satisfying and self-fulfilling: it protects the Left's line and hands PiS an uncontested negotiation.
title: Call him a PiS satellite before he becomes one
subtitle: Clean line, closed door; PiS negotiates with him unopposed
on-arrival: {!
Q.kukiz_channel = 0;
Q.kukiz_programme_credit =
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.kukiz_programme_credit) || 0) - 6);
Q.progressive_credibility += 3;
Q.pis_relation -= 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left says Kukiz has already chosen his side";
!}

We say the obvious thing, which is that a man whose deputies vote with the
government on Europe is not an opposition, and that the circle he has just
registered is a waiting room.

It is a good line and it may well be true by Christmas. It is also the reason
that when Kaczyński calls him in July, there is nobody else in the queue.

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@kukiz_leave_alone
