@kukiz_negotiation
# prose-audit: Grade A — The Kaczyński–Kukiz agreement is decided by programmatic concessions rather than by office, by the player's own bid, and by the relationships built since June; all three outcomes are reachable and each one sets up a different August.
call: poland_normalize
title: Kaczyński needs a second source of votes
subtitle: Kukiz will sell support for institutional promises and not for ministries; Lewica can bid against PiS or watch
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-new-deputies-2023.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.kukiz_negotiation_done = 1;
// PiS pays in programme because that is the only currency Kukiz accepts. How
// much it offers depends on how badly it needs him, which is a function of how
// far Gowin has already gone.
const gowinRisk =
    (100 - Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Number(Q.gowin_standing) || 50))) * 0.2 +
    (Q.republikanie_formed ? 14 : 0) +
    Math.max(0, 60 - Math.max(0, Number(Q.united_right_cohesion) || 55)) * 0.5;
Q.kukiz_pis_offer = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(24 + gowinRisk)));
Q.kukiz_left_bid = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.kukiz_channel) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.kukiz_programme_credit) || 0) * 0.6
)));
Q.news_headline =
    "Nowogrodzka opens negotiations with a man it spent six years mocking";
!}

= July 2021 — The second majority

<span class="party party-pis"><b>Jarosław Kaczyński</b></span> invites <span
class="party party-kukiz"><b>Paweł Kukiz</b></span> to a series of meetings that
both sides describe afterwards as programmatic. They are. <span class="party
party-kukiz"><b>Kukiz</b></span> does not want a ministry,
has publicly refused the offer of one before, and regards the normal currency
of Polish coalition politics — a department, a state company, a deputy
ministership for a friend — as the thing he entered politics to abolish.

What he wants is a list: judges of peace, a referendum act that lowers the
signature threshold, an anti-corruption package with asset declarations that
bite, and changes to the electoral law. <span class="party party-pis"><b>PiS</b></span>
can promise all of it cheaply because promising is not passing, and <span
class="party party-kukiz"><b>Kukiz</b></span> knows that too, which is why the
negotiation is about sequencing rather than about principle.

The reason it is happening now is <span class="party party-agreement"><b>Jarosław
Gowin</b></span>. [? if republikanie_formed = 1: Half of <span class="party
party-agreement"><b>Porozumienie</b></span> is already a different party sitting on the government benches,
and the half that is left is led by a man who has started using the word
"opposition" in interviews.?][? if republikanie_formed = 0: <span class="party
party-agreement"><b>Porozumienie</b></span>
survived its rebellion intact, which from Nowogrodzka's point of view is the
bad outcome: <span class="party party-agreement"><b>Gowin</b></span> now speaks
for eleven deputies and has begun costing the
Polish Deal.?] <span class="party party-pis"><b>Kaczyński</b></span> has decided
that he needs a majority that does not depend on <span class="party
party-agreement"><b>Jarosław Gowin</b></span>, and there is exactly one place to
get one.

[? if kukiz_left_bid >= 30: We are not a spectator in this. The work since June
means <span class="party party-kukiz"><b>Kukiz</b></span>'s people take our calls, and there is a version of the next fortnight
in which the anti-corruption package he wants gets written by us instead.?]
[? if kukiz_left_bid < 30: We have no relationship with him worth the name, and
the negotiation will be conducted without an opposition in the room.?]

- @kukiz_bid_hard
- @kukiz_bid_mixed_jow
- @kukiz_bid_full_jow
- @kukiz_bid_institutions
- @kukiz_expose_deal
- @kukiz_stand_aside

@kukiz_bid_mixed_jow
title: Put Kukiz's 230 plus 230 plan into an Article 96 bill
subtitle: Requires an established channel. Half proportional lists, half single-member districts; no resource cost now, but a constitutional campaign follows.
choose-if: kukiz_channel >= 20
unavailable-subtitle: We need a working relationship with Kukiz's circle before offering to rewrite the Sejm electoral system together.
on-arrival: {!
Q.electoral_reform_proposal = "mixed_230";
Q.electoral_reform_stage = "kukiz_pact";
Q.electoral_reform_result = "Lewica and Kukiz agreed to pursue 230 list seats and 230 JOW seats";
Q.kukiz_left_bid = Math.min(100, Math.max(
    Number(Q.kukiz_left_bid) || 0,
    (Number(Q.kukiz_pis_offer) || 24) + 8
));
Q.kukiz_programme_credit = (Number(Q.kukiz_programme_credit) || 0) + 24;
Q.kukiz_channel = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.kukiz_channel) || 0) + 18);
Q.party_unity -= 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 8;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.news_headline = "Lewica offers Kukiz a constitutional 230-plus-230 electoral pact";
!}

<span class="party party-kukiz"><b>Kukiz</b></span> expected another anti-corruption package with a generous timetable. We
put down an amendment to Article 96 instead: half the Sejm would still come
from proportional lists, while 230 members would be elected directly from
single-member constituencies. It is his own proposal, with somebody finally
offering the votes and legal work required to make it more than a slogan.

Our organisers understand the danger immediately. The proportional half keeps
a national route for smaller parties; the district half rewards whoever can
coordinate candidates and build local machines. <span class="party
party-kukiz"><b>Kukiz</b></span> signs before either side
has time to reconsider what winning the argument would do to it.

- @kukiz_resolution

@kukiz_bid_full_jow
title: Offer Kukiz all 460 Sejm seats through JOW
subtitle: Requires an established channel. One round, one member per district, and a much larger revolt inside the Left.
choose-if: kukiz_channel >= 20
unavailable-subtitle: We need a working relationship with Kukiz's circle before offering the constitutional gamble he has demanded for years.
on-arrival: {!
Q.electoral_reform_proposal = "fptp_460";
Q.electoral_reform_stage = "kukiz_pact";
Q.electoral_reform_result = "Lewica and Kukiz agreed to pursue 460 single-member plurality districts";
Q.kukiz_left_bid = Math.min(100, Math.max(
    Number(Q.kukiz_left_bid) || 0,
    (Number(Q.kukiz_pis_offer) || 24) + 12
));
Q.kukiz_programme_credit = (Number(Q.kukiz_programme_credit) || 0) + 34;
Q.kukiz_channel = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.kukiz_channel) || 0) + 24);
Q.party_unity -= 7;
Q.progressives_dissent += 15;
Q.razem_dissent += 12;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 7;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.news_headline = "Lewica offers Kukiz a 460-seat JOW constitution";
!}

We go further than the compromise <span class="party party-kukiz"><b>Kukiz</b></span>
took to <span class="party party-pis"><b>PiS</b></span>. Every Sejm seat would be
filled in one round from one equal-population constituency. Party lists and
national thresholds disappear; candidate pacts, local organisation and the
ability to finish first become the electoral system.

<span class="party party-kukiz"><b>Kukiz</b></span> accepts on the spot. <span
class="party party-razem"><b>Razem</b></span> calls it voluntary political disarmament,
progressive MPs ask which six cities are supposed to save the parliamentary
Left, and the leadership answers that a promise this large is exactly why
<span class="party party-kukiz"><b>Kukiz</b></span> now walks away from <span
class="party party-pis"><b>Kaczyński</b></span>.

- @kukiz_resolution

@kukiz_bid_hard
# prose-audit: Grade A — Outbidding PiS on Kukiz's own agenda is the strongest way to deny the government a replacement majority and it commits Lewica to legislation it will be held to, including a referendum threshold most of its caucus opposes.
title: Outbid Nowogrodzka on his own programme
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources and a commitment we will be held to; the best chance of denying PiS a second majority
choose-if: resources >= 2 and kukiz_channel >= 20
unavailable-subtitle: Requires two party resources and an existing working relationship with his circle.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.kukiz_left_bid = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.kukiz_left_bid) || 0) + 30);
Q.kukiz_programme_credit =
    (Number(Q.kukiz_programme_credit) || 0) + 18;
Q.kukiz_channel = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.kukiz_channel) || 0) + 16);
Q.left_referendum_commitment = 1;
Q.progressives_dissent += 6;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left puts a joint anti-corruption bill on Kukiz's desk";
!}

We table the package rather than discussing it: declarations, the register, real
inquiry powers, and a referendum threshold we would not have chosen, cosigned
and ready. It is a bill he can hold up at a press conference, which is worth
more to him than a ministry and costs us a fight in our own caucus about
plebiscites.

Nowogrodzka now has to actually pass something instead of promising it.

- @kukiz_resolution

@kukiz_bid_institutions
# prose-audit: Grade A — The narrow bid is the affordable version: it buys Kukiz's anti-corruption agenda without Lewica endorsing referendums or judges of peace, and it moves the outcome less.
title: Offer only the anti-corruption half
subtitle: Cheaper and honest; a smaller claim on his loyalty
choose-if: kukiz_channel >= 10
unavailable-subtitle: We have no channel into his circle to make an offer through.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kukiz_left_bid = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.kukiz_left_bid) || 0) + 14);
Q.kukiz_programme_credit =
    (Number(Q.kukiz_programme_credit) || 0) + 8;
Q.progressive_credibility += 1;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left backs Kukiz's asset declarations and refuses his referendums";
!}

We support the parts we believe in and say plainly which parts we do not. He
does not get a partner; he gets a reliable co-signature on half his programme
and an opposition that has not lied to him about the other half.

It is a smaller offer. It is also the only one we can still defend in front of
our own members.

- @kukiz_resolution

@kukiz_expose_deal
# prose-audit: Grade B — Attacking the negotiation raises its price for both sides: it makes a formal alignment more embarrassing for Kukiz and makes him less reachable by us.
title: Make the negotiation itself the story
subtitle: Raises the price of the deal for both of them; ends our own access
on-arrival: {!
Q.kukiz_channel = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.kukiz_channel) || 0) - 18);
Q.kukiz_left_bid = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.kukiz_left_bid) || 0) - 12);
Q.kukiz_pis_offer = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.kukiz_pis_offer) || 30) - 8);
Q.progressive_credibility += 4;
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left publishes the timetable of the Kaczyński–Kukiz meetings";
!}

We publish the meetings, the dates and the price list, and ask the anti-system
politician to explain what he is getting for six votes. It embarrasses both of
them and it raises the cost of a formal arrangement.

It also means that whatever he does next, he does it without us in the room.

- @kukiz_resolution

@kukiz_stand_aside
# prose-audit: Grade B — Declining the auction is defensible and leaves the outcome entirely to the two negotiating parties, which usually means PiS gets what it came for.
title: Refuse to bid for a man who mocks the left
subtitle: Nothing spent; the negotiation resolves without us
on-arrival: {!
Q.kukiz_left_bid = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.kukiz_left_bid) || 0) - 6);
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left declines to compete for Kukiz's votes";
!}

We are not going to spend the summer bidding for the affection of a man whose
central political conviction is that people like us are the problem. If the
government wants him, the government can have him and can own him.

- @kukiz_resolution

@kukiz_resolution
# prose-audit: Grade A — The three outcomes are produced by the offers actually made rather than by the calendar, and each one is stated in the terms that matter in August: whether Kukiz is on the government's list, in its lobby, or in neither.
title: What Kukiz agreed to
subtitle: A current of PiS, a toleration that can be withdrawn, or nothing
on-arrival: {!
const offer = Math.max(0, Number(Q.kukiz_pis_offer) || 24);
const bid = Math.max(0, Number(Q.kukiz_left_bid) || 0);
const hostility = Math.max(0, 40 - Math.max(0, Number(Q.kukiz_channel) || 0));
const kukiz = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "kukiz15";
});
if (offer >= 44 && bid < offer - 8 && hostility >= 18) {
    Q.kukiz_alignment = "pis_current";
} else if (bid >= offer + 6) {
    Q.kukiz_alignment = "refused";
} else if (offer >= 30) {
    Q.kukiz_alignment = "toleration";
} else {
    Q.kukiz_alignment = "refused";
}
if (kukiz) {
    if (Q.kukiz_alignment == "pis_current") {
        kukiz.support_mode = "coalition";
        kukiz.allied = 1;
        kukiz.relation = Math.max(-100, (Number(kukiz.relation) || 12) - 10);
        kukiz.legal_status = "independent party aligned with the United Right";
        kukiz.electoral_outside_option = "places on the PiS list";
        kukiz.list_committee = "pis";
        Q.kukiz_list_committee = "pis";
        Q.government_support_seats =
            (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 235) +
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.kukiz_seats) || 0);
        Q.news_headline =
            "Kukiz'15 agrees to sustain the government in exchange for its programme";
    } else if (Q.kukiz_alignment == "toleration") {
        kukiz.support_mode = "toleration";
        kukiz.allied = 0;
        kukiz.legal_status = "independent party tolerating the government";
        kukiz.electoral_outside_option = "no committee agreed for the next term";
        Q.kukiz_list_committee = "kukiz";
        Q.news_headline =
            "Kukiz will vote for the budget and for nothing he has not been paid for";
    } else {
        kukiz.support_mode = "opposition";
        kukiz.allied = 0;
        kukiz.relation = Math.min(100, (Number(kukiz.relation) || 12) + 8);
        kukiz.legal_status = "independent party outside every camp";
        kukiz.electoral_outside_option = "an independent committee or none";
        Q.kukiz_list_committee = "kukiz";
        Q.news_headline =
            "Kukiz refuses Kaczyński and the government's arithmetic gets worse";
    }
}
!}

= The terms

[? if kukiz_alignment = "pis_current": Kukiz'15 will support the Polish Deal,
the budget and the government's flagship legislation. In exchange PiS commits,
on paper, to judges of peace, a referendum act and an anti-corruption package,
in that order and on a timetable that conveniently begins after the tax reform
has passed. He remains a separate registered party with his own leader, his own
circle and his own name; he is now also a component of the governing camp and,
when the lists are filed, will very probably be on Prawo i Sprawiedliwość's. Kaczyński has bought a replacement majority for the price of a legislative
programme he intended to pass slowly or not at all.?]
[? if kukiz_alignment = "toleration": Kukiz'15 will vote for the budget, for
confidence, and for individual bills it has been paid for in advance. It will
vote against everything else and it reserves the right to decide which is
which on the morning. There is no coalition, no list agreement and no
commitment past the next roll call. It is the most Kukiz outcome available: transactional, renewable and useless
for planning. The government has bought votes rather than a majority, and it
will have to buy them again.?]
[? if kukiz_alignment = "refused": Kukiz walks. Either PiS would not put
anything real on paper or somebody else got there first, and the circle
announces that it is not for sale to a government that has spent six years
promising the same four bills. Nowogrodzka is now in the position it spent the spring trying to avoid: its
majority depends on Jarosław Gowin, and Jarosław Gowin has started giving
interviews about the Polish Deal.?]
[? if kukiz_alignment = "refused" and electoral_reform_proposal = "mixed_230":
The somebody else is us. Kukiz leaves with a signed 230-plus-230 Article 96
draft and a December appointment with the parties whose votes would be needed
to reach a constitutional majority.?]
[? if kukiz_alignment = "refused" and electoral_reform_proposal = "fptp_460":
The somebody else is us. Kukiz leaves with a signed promise of 460
single-member districts and a project that can survive only if both large
parties decide they expect to win it.?]

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign
